1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,720
This is the most important step: connecting your tablet to your PC.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,630
You only need to do it once.

3
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:13,021
Before connecting, make sure your PC and your tablet are on the same Wi-Fi network,

4
00:00:13,021 --> 00:00:15,626
and that PadDeck is running on the PC.

5
00:00:15,626 --> 00:00:19,740
Guest networks usually block devices from seeing each other.

6
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:24,778
On your PC, open PadDeck and click Devices in the sidebar.

7
00:00:24,778 --> 00:00:29,416
Here you'll find a large QR code and a six digit pairing code.

8
00:00:29,416 --> 00:00:33,380
Each code works once, and expires after five minutes.

9
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,172
On the tablet, open PadDeck.

10
00:00:36,172 --> 00:00:39,161
You'll see the Pair with your PC screen.

11
00:00:39,161 --> 00:00:44,540
Tap Scan QR code, and point the camera at the QR code on your PC screen.

12
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:49,308
Or, tap your PC in the list of PCs found on this network,

13
00:00:49,308 --> 00:00:52,020
and type the six digits on the keypad.

14
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:55,660
Pairing starts as soon as you enter the last digit.

15
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:59,285
When pairing succeeds, your buttons appear.

16
00:00:59,285 --> 00:01:04,795
Look at the top: a green dot, and the word Connected, mean everything is working.

17
00:01:04,795 --> 00:01:09,420
The number shows how many milliseconds a tap takes to reach your PC.

18
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:15,249
On the PC, your tablet now appears under Paired devices, with a green dot.

19
00:01:15,249 --> 00:01:18,090
You can remove a device here at any time.

20
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:23,223
If it doesn't connect, check both devices use the same Wi-Fi,

21
00:01:23,223 --> 00:01:29,256
make sure PadDeck is running, and click Allow through firewall on the Devices page.

22
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:31,872
If the code expired, press New code.

23
00:01:31,872 --> 00:01:36,669
An amber dot means connecting or slow, and red means disconnected.

24
00:01:36,669 --> 00:01:39,140
PadDeck keeps retrying on its own.

